waylandsink: ignore repeated wl_output.done in output_done

output_done() takes the GstWlDisplay with g_object_steal_data(), so it is
NULL from the second "done" event on. Compositors send "done" again when an
output changes - sway does on every "output * power on" (screen wake) - and
every waylandsink then segfaulted in g_mutex_lock(NULL->outputs_mutex)
("GstWlDisplay[...]: segfault at ffffffffffffffa8 ... in libglib").

Return early instead: the output is registered on its first "done", and
later property updates reach the GstWlOutput through its own listeners.
(Keeping the pointer and re-running g_hash_table_replace() would unref the
same output through the table's value destroy function on every "done".)
Upstream: gstreamer#5144, #5329.

--- a/gst-libs/gst/wayland/gstwldisplay.c
+++ b/gst-libs/gst/wayland/gstwldisplay.c
@@ -431,9 +431,14 @@
 {
   GstWlOutput *output = GST_WL_OUTPUT (data);
   GstWlDisplay *self = g_object_steal_data (G_OBJECT (output), "display");
-  GstWlDisplayPrivate *priv = gst_wl_display_get_instance_private (self);
+  GstWlDisplayPrivate *priv;
   const gchar *name = gst_wl_output_get_name (output);
 
+  /* already registered on the first done (the pointer was stolen then) */
+  if (!self)
+    return;
+  priv = gst_wl_display_get_instance_private (self);
+
   GST_INFO ("Adding output %s (%p):", name, wl_output);
   GST_INFO ("  Make:       %s", gst_wl_output_get_make (output));
   GST_INFO ("  Model:      %s", gst_wl_output_get_model (output));
